From: illumos-drm <illumos-drm@code.aopc.cloud>
Subject: [PATCH 14] amdgpu: mode setting through misc/drm_kms

On illumos the DRM core (misc/drm_core) owns the ioctl entry, files and
events, and forwards the mode-setting ioctls of a Linux-KMS device to
Linux's KMS code, which misc/drm_kms carries (facade 2.0, drm_lkms.h).
amdgpu_kms_driver points its illumos_lkms at misc/drm_kms' hook table
(drm_kms_illumos_funcs), as i915n's display build does (i915n patch
0012). amdgpu's own mode-setting code (amdgpu_display.c, dce_v6_0.c on
Southern Islands; no DC in this build) already runs at probe; without
the hook the core reported no mode-setting capabilities and refused the
mode-setting ioctls. The illumos console is not taken over here: a GPU
that drives the console needs that first (not yet done).

The partition driver (amdgpu_partition_driver, for XCP partitions on
newer chips) has no DRIVER_MODESET and stays without the hook.

License: a preprocessor-guarded declaration and initialiser in an MIT
file; applied to the pinned Linux tree.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_drv.c
@@ -3112,9 +3112,19 @@
 	DRM_IOCTL_DEF_DRV(AMDGPU_GEM_LIST_HANDLES, amdgpu_gem_list_handles_ioctl, DRM_AUTH|DRM_RENDER_ALLOW),
 };
 
+#ifdef __illumos__
+/*
+ * misc/drm_kms: Linux's KMS code behind the DRM core (facade 2.0,
+ * drm_lkms.h). The core forwards the mode-setting ioctls of this device
+ * to it once the LinuxKPI layer's drm_dev_register() starts mode setting.
+ */
+extern const struct drm_illumos_lkms_funcs drm_kms_illumos_funcs;
+#endif
+
 static const struct drm_driver amdgpu_kms_driver = {
 #ifdef __illumos__
 	DRM_FACADE_DRIVER_VERSION,
+	.illumos_lkms = &drm_kms_illumos_funcs,
 	/*
 	 * No DRM core object size limit (256 MiB by default):
 	 * amdgpu_bo_validate_size() limits an object to the size of its
